.TH BROWSER 1
.SH NAME
browser, servoshell, webfs-rs \- web browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B browser
[
.I url
]
.PP
.B servoshell
[
.I url
]
.PP
.B webfs-rs
[
.B -dD
] [
.B -A
.I useragent
] [
.B -T
.I timeout
] [
.B -m
.I mtpt
] [
.B -s
.I service
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Browser
shows the web page
.I url
in the window it runs in, with
.IR servoshell ,
Servo's own browser (Servo for 9space: Servo with SpiderMonkey, drawing through
Mesa's Zink on the window system's GPU,
.IR wsys (4)).
It runs in
.IR wsys ;
the address bar takes a new
.I url
(Ctrl-L).
.PP
Servo's requests go through
.IR webfs-rs ,
a version of
.IR webfs (4)
with extensions Servo needs: several messages a write of
.BR ctl ,
redirects and cookies left to Servo, and a client's
.B head
file, which marks it.
.I Browser
mounts one on
.B /mnt/web
in a private name space; the
.I webfs
on
.B /mnt/web
of the rest stays as it was.
.PP
.I Webfs-rs
mounts itself on
.I mtpt
(default
.BR /mnt/web )
and, with
.BR -s ,
posts itself as
.BI /srv/ service
too;
.B -s
alone only posts it.
.I Browser
starts it so, in a name space of its own, mounts the post and removes it:
.I webfs-rs
ends with its last mount, when the browser ends, however it ends.
Against a
.I webfs
without the extensions,
.I servoshell
refuses its requests, once, with an error.
.PP
It needs the network configured
.RI ( ipconfig (8))
and a resolver
.RI ( ndb (8)'s
.IR dns ),
as the installed system does at boot; a live CD does not (run
.B ip/ipconfig
and
.BR "ndb/dns -r" ).
Without them every page fails with
.BR "bad status """"" .
.PP
The certificates of the authorities it trusts for
.B https
are in
.BR /sys/lib/tls/ca.pem .
Fonts come from
.IR fontconfig 's
configuration,
.BR /lib/fontconfig/fonts.conf
(the TrueType fonts of
.BR /lib/font/ttf ).
.SH FILES
.TF /sys/lib/browser/SOURCES
.TP
.B /sys/lib/browser/LICENSES.md
which part of the programs is under which licence
.TP
.B /sys/lib/browser/LICENSE.MPL-2.0
the Mozilla Public License 2.0, Servo's and SpiderMonkey's
.TP
.B /sys/lib/browser/SOURCES
where their source code is
.TP
.B /sys/lib/browser/resources
.IR servoshell 's
own pages
.RB ( servo:newtab ,
a new tab's, and the others;
.B $servoresources
names another directory)
.TP
.B $home/lib/servo
.IR servoshell 's
settings
.RB ( /tmp/servo
where the home cannot be written, as on the live CD)
.TP
.B /tmp/browser.webfs.log
.IR webfs-rs 's
errors
.SH SOURCE
.B /rc/bin/browser
.br
9space's browser repository (not in
.BR /sys/src :
Servo and SpiderMonkey are under the MPL, the tree takes only permissive code;
.B /sys/lib/browser/SOURCES
says where)
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR webfs (4),
.IR wsys (4),
.IR ipconfig (8)
.SH BUGS
Memory grows with each page visited (in 9space's first long test about 57 MB a
page, kept in the program's heap): restart
.I browser
after long sessions.
.PP
One process: Servo's content runs in
.IR servoshell 's
own (no
.BR --multiprocess ).
The system's time zone is UTC to it.
.SH HISTORY
9space's.
